('h2', "11.7  Stages of Team Development \u2014 Tuckman's Model (1965)"),
('p', "**This is highly examinable.** Learn the five stages in order, with a one-line description and the leader's task in each."),
('flow', ["**1. FORMING** \u2014 Members meet, are polite, anxious and dependent on the leader. Roles and goals are unclear; there is little real work. *Leader's task:* **direct** \u2014 introduce, clarify goals, roles and ground rules.",
          "**2. STORMING** \u2014 Conflict emerges over roles, authority, methods and status; cliques form; morale may dip; some resist the task. *Leader's task:* **coach** \u2014 surface and resolve conflict, re-clarify roles, keep the focus on the goal. **This stage is normal and necessary \u2014 not a failure.**",
          "**3. NORMING** \u2014 Norms, trust and cohesion develop; roles are accepted; the team begins to cooperate and to give feedback constructively. *Leader's task:* **support and facilitate**; reinforce standards.",
          "**4. PERFORMING** \u2014 The team is mature, interdependent, motivated and highly productive; it solves problems itself; leadership is shared. *Leader's task:* **delegate**; remove obstacles; develop members.",
          "**5. ADJOURNING (Mourning)** \u2014 Added by Tuckman and Jensen (1977). The team disbands after achieving its purpose; members feel loss. *Leader's task:* **recognise, celebrate, evaluate, document learning and reassign** people well."]),
('mne', ("\u201CForm \u2013 Storm \u2013 Norm \u2013 Perform \u2013 Adjourn\u201D",
         ["A rhyming sequence that is easy to reproduce under exam pressure. Add the leader's role in each: **Direct \u2192 Coach \u2192 Support \u2192 Delegate \u2192 Close** (which conveniently matches Hersey & Blanchard's situational leadership)."])),

